  "description": "Here's your chance to check\nout the finest dual suspension design without getting a second mortgage\non the farm. The Diamond Lite 1 features a rebound-adjustable coil spring\nshock and SunTour Magnesium EXR fork for economy. Like the Diamond Lite\n2, the frame is made with 7005 butted aluminum tubing, accepts the Twin\nTechnology linkage, is disc brake-ready and the rear suspension pivots\non sealed bearings. That's quite a package for a bike with a three-digit\nprice tag.\n\nThis is an easy bike to add to your collection if you already own a hard\ntail. But if you're a first-time buyer, you're probably weighing the pros\nand cons of dual versus front suspension. The best way to make up your\nmind is to put this catalog down and go straight to your friendly neighborhood\nFuji dealer for a test ride. Talk is talk, but a test ride is real data.\nUnfortunately, you probably won't be able to make a thorough off-road\ncomparison. But the performance and handling differences, even in the\nstore parking lot, should be great enough to help you get off the fence.\n\nOr stay there. It's a great excuse for buying another bike later.",
